    "lawCode": "Amd §103, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4284\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to the location\nof open meetings\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo ensure that public bodies make a reasonable effort to hold public\nmeetings in a room which can accommodate members of the public who\nwish to attend.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 103 of the public officers law is amended by adding a new\nsubdivision (d).\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe purpose of the NYS open meetings law is to guarantee that public\nbusiness be performed in an open and public manner. Open meetings\nallow NYS citizens to observe their elected officials and the\ndecisions that go into the making of public policy.  Public attendance\nis essential to the democratic process.\n\nCurrent law does not stipulate that these meetings must be held in an\nadequately sizeable room. It is still possible for members of the\npublic to be shut out while the letter of the law is being observed.\nThis bill explicitly requires that the room be of ample size to\naccommodate those who wish to attend an \"open\" meeting.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2005-06: A.3032 - Passed Assembly\n2007-08: A.6013 - Third Reading Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
